INT. MIRROR VAULT OF THE DROWNED KING - NIGHT

A cavern of black glass. Ten thousand mirrors cover walls, floor, ceiling. Torchlight multiplies into a bonfire of stars. Every reflection moves a half-second late.

SORREL, thirties, a thief in a hooded cloak, creeps along a narrow ledge of obsidian. She clutches a leather satchel. She stops. Her reflection stops, then.

SORREL
(muttering)
Don't look. Don't look.

She looks. The reflections grin.

SORREL (CONT'D)
(to the vault)
I'm only here for the crown! You can keep the rest!

Silence. A single mirror cracks, a thin white line.

SORREL (CONT'D)
(to herself)
Brilliant. Wake the whole place.

She steps off the ledge onto a dais. A crown of black pearl rests on a pillow of bone. She reaches for it.

BRIGID (O.S.)
Don't.

Sorrel spins. A figure steps out of a mirror, not around it, out of it, as a swimmer climbs from a pool.

BRIGID, forties, tall, in a silver surcoat, a long sword in one hand. Her face is the same as Sorrel's, older, scarred across the brow.

SORREL
Who are you?

BRIGID
You. After you take it.

They stare at each other. Torches gutter.

SORREL
(to the vault)
Is she real?

BRIGID
Don't bother. The vault doesn't answer.

SORREL
(muttering)
That's the first honest thing I've heard in a week.

Brigid raises the sword. Sorrel pulls a short knife. They circle the dais, each step mirrored a thousand times.

BRIGID
Put the knife down.

SORREL
Put the sword down.

BRIGID
I won't.

SORREL
Then neither will I.

They lunge together. Steel rings. Sorrel ducks, rolls under Brigid's blade. Brigid whirls and kicks the knife from her grip. It skitters across the glass. Both lunge for it. Both reach it. Both freeze, hands on the hilt.

BRIGID
Let go.

SORREL
You let go.

BRIGID
(quiet)
I wore this knife the night I took the crown. It cost me a sister.

SORREL
I don't have a sister.

BRIGID
You will.

Sorrel's grip loosens. Brigid's too. The knife lies between them.

SORREL
(to the whole vault)
Someone tell me what's happening!

The mirrors all go dark, one after another, like candles. Only two torches remain. In their light the women stand on the dais, panting.

BRIGID
It's the king's last trick. It shows you what you'll become.

SORREL
(muttering)
Wonderful. A warning with a sword.

BRIGID
Leave the crown. Walk out.

SORREL
And you?

BRIGID
I'll vanish. Like I always do.

Sorrel looks at the crown. At Brigid. At the dark glass.

SORREL
(to herself)
Fine.

She steps back from the dais. Slings her satchel over her shoulder. Brigid lowers the sword.

BRIGID
Thank you.

SORREL
Don't thank me. I want a better offer next time.

Brigid smiles, sad, and steps backward into a mirror. It swallows her. The crown stays on its bone pillow.

Sorrel exits along the ledge. At the cavern's mouth she stops, glances back once. Her reflection nods.
